{"id": "da31ef80-3554-49d7-819e-608a22e416ab", "card": {"foregroundColor": {"blue": 1, "green": 1, "opacity": 1, "red": 1}, "image": "", "imageStyle": "textFirst", "localizedTitle": {"en": "### 2020 COVID-19\n\n**Mobility Lockdown**\n", "es": "### 2020 COVID-19\n\n**Confinamiento**\n", "pt": "### 2020 COVID-19\n\n**Isolamento Social**\n"}}, "pages": [{"id": "f34a38d2-b4c2-4cfd-9d29-8c0c6f9cbeac", "blocks": [{"id": "dd65b643-2990-404b-a64e-c8c28a32151c", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Before the lockdown", "es": "## Antes del confinamiento", "pt": "## Antes do isolamento"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "d72c567c-a33a-4030-b397-66736617031e", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "During the winter of 2020 cities around the world locked down on people's\nmobility to counter the viral spread of COVID-19.\n\nThis led to reductions\\\nin high-frequency seismic noise, a substantial part of which is caused by\nhuman industriousness.\n\nOn the contrary, Earth's oceans continued to produce\nlower frequency seismic noise, which often overpowers other noise and sounds\nlike running water or a steady stream of static or white noise, depending\non the octaves higher.\n", "es": "Durante el invierno de 2020 las ciudades del mundo fueron confinadas para\ncontrarrestar la propagaci\u00f3n del virus COVID-19.\n\nEsto condujo a reducciones del ruido s\u00edsmico de alta frecuencia, del cual,\nuna parte sustancial es causado por la actividad industrial.\n\nPor el contrario, los oc\u00e9anos de la tierra continuaron produciendo ruido s\u00edsmico\nde baja frecuencia, que a menudo supera a otros ruidos, y que suena como agua\ncorriente o como flujo constante de ruido est\u00e1tico o blanco, seg\u00fan el incremento\nde octavas.\n", "pt": "Durante o inverno de 2020 (no hemisf\u00e9rio norte), as cidades ao redor do mundo \nforam colocadas em isolamento para conter a propaga\u00e7\u00e3o do v\u00edrus da COVID-19. \n\nIsso causou uma redu\u00e7\u00e3o no ru\u00eddo s\u00edsmico de alta frequ\u00eancia, que \u00e9 gerado em \ngrande parte pela atividade industrial. \n\nPor outro lado, os oceanos terrestres continuaram produzindo ru\u00eddo s\u00edsmico de baixa \nfrequ\u00eancia, que muitas vezes supera outros tipos de ru\u00eddo e soa como \u00e1gua corrente \nou como um fluxo constante de ru\u00eddo est\u00e1tico ou branco, dependendo do aumento das oitavas.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "d5edfdcf-f2b3-4740-bf20-8c16d38ed423", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Let's listen to 4 hours of seismic noise from a Monday evening in \n**Po Shan, Hong Kong**. First we will listen to the Monday before the lockdown.\n", "es": "Escuchemos 4 horas de ruido s\u00edsmico un lunes por la tarde en **Po Shan,\nHong Kong**. Primero, escuchemos un lunes antes del confinamiento.\n", "pt": "Vamos escutar 4 horas de ru\u00eddo s\u00edsmico de uma tarde de segunda-feira\nem **Po Shan, Hong Kong**. Primeiro escutaremos \u00e0 segunda-feira antes\ndo isolamento social.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "7a812ca6-9cf5-4a7e-ab7d-32b13ce776de", "octavesHigher": 1024, "type": "localWave", "volumeModifier": "fixed", "waveData": {"duration": 14400, "startDate": "2020-01-20T07:00:00Z", "station": {"group": "user", "id": "7F181F18-B063-49A3-80BB-F2EABCF95024", "name": "Po Shan, Hong Kong", "periods": [{"channel": "BHZ", "location": "00", "network": "HK", "station": "HKPS"}], "preferredTimeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}, "timeLatency": 0}, "timeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}}}, {"id": "f7bf126f-189b-4044-abae-93b19dbc52ea", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Did you hear that steady backgrounds noise that always bounces around the\nEarth?\n\nDid you also hear the odd sounds during the midst of evening rush hour in\nHong Kong?\n\nThey sound like horns or party favor blowouts. These are part of the high\nfrequency noise that reduced during lockdown.\n", "es": "\u00bfEscuchaste ese ruido de fondo constante que siempre rebota alrededor de\nla Tierra?\n\n\u00bfEscuchaste tambi\u00e9n sonidos extra\u00f1os durante la hora punta de la noche en\nHong Kong?\n\nSuenan como bocinas o explosiones. Estos forman parte del ruido de alta frecuencia\nque se redujo durante el confinamiento.\n", "pt": "Voc\u00ea escutou esse ru\u00eddo de fundo constante que sempre reverbera ao redor da Terra?\n\nVoc\u00ea tamb\u00e9m ouviu os sons estranhos em meio ao hor\u00e1rio de pico noturno em Hong Kong?\n\nParecem buzinas ou estalidos. Eles s\u00e3o parte do ru\u00eddo de alta frequ\u00eancia que diminuiu \ndurante o confinamento.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "f214a36b-19cc-4c6e-9dc2-71d9e4530faf", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Buried in all this natural and human-made noise, at the very beginning\nof the recording are seismic waves from a M6.1 earthquake in the South Sandwich\nIslands. They are even lower in frequency and much easier to hear if you change\nthe octaves higher to 14. The seismic waves from that earthquake then sound\nlike a ping.\n", "es": "Al comienzo de la grabaci\u00f3n, escondidas en todo el ruido natural y el provocado\npor el hombre, se encuentran las ondas s\u00edsmicas de un terremoto M6.1 en las\nIslas Sandwich del Sur. Son incluso m\u00e1s bajas en frecuencia y, si cambias\nel incremento de octavas a 14, mucho m\u00e1s f\u00e1ciles de escuchar. Las ondas s\u00edsmicas\nde ese terremoto suenan como un *ping*.\n", "pt": "Enterradas sob todo esse ru\u00eddo de origem natural e humana, bem no in\u00edcio \nda grava\u00e7\u00e3o, est\u00e3o as ondas s\u00edsmicas de um terremoto de magnitude 6.1 nas Ilhas \nSandwich do Sul. Elas t\u00eam uma frequ\u00eancia ainda mais baixa e ficam muito mais \nf\u00e1ceis de ouvir se voc\u00ea ajustar o aumento de oitavas para 14. As ondas s\u00edsmicas \ndesse terremoto soam como um *ping*.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "f5610f7e-a68d-4726-82a0-d991667c0442", "action": "next", "localizedText": {"en": "Next", "es": "Siguiente", "pt": "Pr\u00f3ximo"}, "paramValue": "", "type": "button"}], "title": "Before"}, {"id": "6876d5a5-3505-4a67-8e0d-0b2a2d556996", "blocks": [{"id": "739f2b20-cf7c-4f12-aff3-f3b7ae0f9461", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## During lockdown", "es": "## Durante el confinamiento", "pt": "## Durante o isolamento"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "708c1e82-6200-4e11-b8b9-43e321dc5317", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Hong Kong began their lockdown on January 25, 2020. The following Monday\nwas much quieter than the Monday you listened to. Except natural noise from\nthe oceans, atmosphere, and the solid Earth itself continued unfettered.\n", "es": "Hong Kong comenz\u00f3 el confinamiento el 25 de enero de 2020. El siguiente\nlunes fue mucho m\u00e1s tranquilo que el lunes que escuchaste, excepto para el\nruido natural de los oc\u00e9anos, la atm\u00f3sfera y la propia Tierra s\u00f3lida, que\ncontinuaron sin restricciones.\n", "pt": "Hong Kong iniciou seu confinamento em 25 de janeiro de 2020. A segunda-feira \nseguinte foi muito mais tranquila do que a segunda-feira que voc\u00ea ouviu, com \nexce\u00e7\u00e3o do ru\u00eddo natural dos oceanos, da atmosfera e da pr\u00f3pria Terra s\u00f3lida, \nque continuaram ocorrendo sem mudan\u00e7as.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "4f4da64c-df86-4006-88f6-868def4765fa", "octavesHigher": 1024, "type": "localWave", "volumeModifier": "fixed", "waveData": {"duration": 14400, "startDate": "2020-01-27T07:00:00Z", "station": {"group": "user", "id": "7F181F18-B063-49A3-80BB-F2EABCF95024", "name": "Po Shan, Hong Kong", "periods": [{"channel": "BHZ", "location": "00", "network": "HK", "station": "HKPS"}], "preferredTimeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}, "timeLatency": 0}, "timeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}}}, {"id": "7896eb5b-7044-429c-aa54-72887f51e055", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Likely you noticed the absence of the high-frequency *honking* noise caused\nby the lockdown. This was the case in many cities around the world. The lowered\nnoise levels allowed seismologists to better see signals from weak, nearby\nearthquakes that occurred during the lockdown.\n", "es": "Es probable que haya notado la ausencia del ruido de *bocina* de alta frecuencia\ncausado por el confinamiento. As\u00ed fue en muchas ciudades del mundo. Los niveles\nde ruido reducidos permitieron a los sism\u00f3logos ver mejor las se\u00f1ales de los\nterremotos d\u00e9biles cercanos que ocurrieron durante el confinamiento.\n", "pt": "Provavelmente voc\u00ea notou a aus\u00eancia do ru\u00eddo de alta frequ\u00eancia das buzinas, causada \npelo isolamento. Isso aconteceu em muitas cidades ao redor do mundo. A redu\u00e7\u00e3o nos \nn\u00edveis de ru\u00eddo permitiu que os sism\u00f3logos observassem melhor os sinais de terremotos \nfracos e pr\u00f3ximos que ocorreram durante o isolamento.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "4c106806-a711-4a03-8be8-cf995719cf1b", "action": "next", "localizedText": {"en": "Next", "es": "Siguiente", "pt": "Pr\u00f3ximo"}, "paramValue": "", "type": "button"}], "title": "After"}, {"id": "17225480-7b79-46b4-8705-1f4443434423", "blocks": [{"id": "460c454b-61af-4dd1-b5b3-a3c7adb3d3de", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Question", "es": "## Pregunta", "pt": "## Pergunta"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "5b5a26b6-8ad0-4b9e-8d4c-774ba926ce25", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Would you like to measure seismic activity generated by human hustle and bustle?\n", "es": "\u00bfTe gustar\u00eda medir la actividad s\u00edsmica generada por el ajetreo y el bullicio humanos?\n", "pt": "Voc\u00ea gostaria de medir a atividade s\u00edsmica gerada pela correria e agita\u00e7\u00e3o humana?\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "f6f99bdf-92c9-469b-a1d8-29304cf59db0", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "If yes, there are many types of educational seismometers that can be placed in schools, \nhomes, and other buildings. They will demonstrate that each day's signal and noise is \nsubtly or significantly different from other days'. \n\nAdditionally, these seismometers are welcomed to join networks, so you can combine data\nfrom your seismometer with those from others. Combining data allows for signal and noise \ncomparisons, tracks waves as they traverse the globe and reveal Earth's layers, and \nlets you determine the epicenter of a recorded earthquake, among other things.\n", "es": "Si la respuesta es s\u00ed, hay muchos tipos de sism\u00f3metros educativos que se pueden \ncolocar en escuelas, hogares y otros edificios. Te demostrar\u00e1n que la se\u00f1al y el ruido \nde cada d\u00eda son sutiles o significativamente diferentes de los de otros d\u00edas.\n\nAdem\u00e1s, estos sism\u00f3metros pueden unirse a redes, lo que permite combinar los datos de \ntu sism\u00f3metro con los de otros. La combinaci\u00f3n de datos permite comparar se\u00f1ales y \nruidos, rastrear ondas mientras atraviesan el globo y revelar las capas de la Tierra y \ntambi\u00e9n te permiten determinar el epicentro de un terremoto registrado, entre otras cosas.\n", "pt": "Caso esteja, existem muitos tipos de sism\u00f4metros educacionais que podem ser instalados em \nescolas, casas e outros edif\u00edcios. Eles demonstram que o sinal e o ru\u00eddo de cada dia podem \nser sutilmente ou significativamente diferentes dos de outros dias.\n\nAl\u00e9m disso, esses sism\u00f4metros s\u00e3o \u00fateis para integrar redes, permitindo combinar \nos dados do seu sism\u00f4metro com os de outros. A combina\u00e7\u00e3o dos dados possibilita compara\u00e7\u00f5es \nentre sinais e ru\u00eddos, rastreamento das ondas enquanto percorrem o planeta e revelam as camadas \nda Terra, al\u00e9m de permitir que determinemos o epicentro de um terremoto registrado, \nentre outras coisas.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false, "unveil": {"unveilText": {"en": "Unveil answer", "es": "Desvelar respuesta", "pt": "Mostrar resposta"}, "waitingTime": 5}}, {"id": "a1881abc-7825-4237-8197-7234abcda503", "action": "close", "localizedText": {"en": "Close", "es": "Cerrar", "pt": "Fechar"}, "paramValue": null, "type": "button"}], "title": "P4.Questions"}], "title": {"en": "2020 COVID-19 Mobility Lockdown"}}